initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}=-4{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ {{field-2}}={{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-4{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{7{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-4L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=7L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+5=-4{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=7{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fdb9ba42-ac1b-55bc-8e22-328134948e48" "answer-field-843ce369-accc-5c77-a81b-aaf1fa3a134a" "answer-field-7806e24d-5f36-5b01-8321-41ffabff4998"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fdb9ba42-ac1b-55bc-8e22-328134948e48" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdb9ba42-ac1b-55bc-8e22-328134948e48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-497a2587-af32-58f2-acc6-994ca52456f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-497a2587-af32-58f2-acc6-994ca52456f1" "answer-8afd5501-c776-5ccb-8d97-3273464ca9f4" "answer-712e42fa-7b12-5974-bec3-df3b2a35d9c1" "answer-661bf31f-47bf-5dcd-856c-f898061b2ff8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-497a2587-