ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{2}(s)-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7806e24d-5f36-5b01-8321-41ffabff4998" :answer-field/id #uuid "7806e24d-5f36-5b01-8321-41ffabff4998" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b8c5ad7c-5fb8-550d-b68d-996cbdc50fd4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7135ebc0-5a1b-5fa4-a805-14e601305649" "answer-c8e7a505-53cb-53de-83a6-baaf8c95c51b" "answer-b8c5ad7c-5fb8-550d-b68d-996cbdc50fd4" "answer-0159502e-a9cf-5ff7-bff6-d0e20f2c8963"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7135ebc0-5a1b-5fa4-a805-14e601305649" :answer/id #uuid "7135ebc0-5a1b-5fa4-a805-14e601305649" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8e7a505-53cb-53de-83a6-baaf8c95c51b" :answer/id #uuid "c8e7a505-53cb-53de-83a6-baaf8c95c51b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8c5ad7c-5fb8-550d-b68d-996cbdc50fd4" :answer/id #uuid "b8c5ad7c-5fb8-550d-b68d-996cbdc50fd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0159502e-a9cf-5ff7-bff6-d0e20f2c8963" :answer/id #uuid "0159502e-a9cf-5ff7-bff6-d0e20f2c8963" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167163 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-9={X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-6=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)=9 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-2){X}_{2}(s)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s)]+2{X}_{2}(s) & =9 \\\\ 6(s-1)-[(s-1)(s-2)-2]{X}_{2}(s) & =9 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-3s){X}_{2}(s) & =9-6(s-1) \\\\ -s(s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =-6s+15 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =6-(s-2)\\cdot \\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6s(s-3)-3(s-2)(2s-5)}{s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(3s-10)}{s(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(3s-10)}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-a9551a40-c332-54a5-8337-fb6b102278bb" :question/id #uuid "a9551a40-c332-54a5-8337-fb6b102278bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-332029" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-6(s-1)}{s(s-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=2{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+6=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-2){X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)=3 \\\\ 2{X}_{1}(s)+(s-1){X}_{2}(s)=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-6-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-2)[\\frac{-6-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}]+{X}_{2}(s) & =3 \\\\ (s-2)[-6-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)]+2{X}_{2}(s) & =6 \\\\ -6(s-2)-(s-2)(s-1){X}_{2}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) & =6 \\\\ [-(s-2)(s-1)+2]{X}_{2}(s) & =6+6(s-2) \\\\ (-{s}^{2}+3s){X}_{2}(s) & =6s-6 \\\\ -s(s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =6(s-1) \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-6(s-1)}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-6-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6-(s-1)(\\frac{-6(s-1)}{s(s-3)})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6+\\frac{6(s-1)^{2}}{s(s-3)}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6s(s-3)+6(s-1)^{2}}{2s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(s+1)}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(s+1)}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-6(s-1)}{s(s-3)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-feb29a18-3baa-5257-96e8-ae32828c5d44"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-feb29a18-3baa-5257-96e8-ae32828c5d44" :answer-field/id #uuid "feb29a18-3baa-5257-96e8-ae32828c5d44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5b33fffb-189c-5d9f-921e-fb455c3f6d66" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b33fffb-189c-5d9f-921e-fb455c3f6d66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b33fffb-189c-5d9f-921e-fb455c3f6d66" :answer/id #uuid "5b33fffb-189c-5d9f-921e-fb455c3f6d66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3(s+1)}{s(s-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186305034 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+{e}^{2t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167160 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{7/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{7/2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-\\frac{7}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{1\\cdot t}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1/2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7/2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164008 :answer-field/correct "answer-554b6a08-d810-54b8-b391-27bcd47e0847" :answer-field/choices ["answer-554b6a08-d810-54b8-b391-27bcd47e0847"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-554b6a08-d810-54b8-b391-27bcd47e0847" :answer/id #uuid "554b6a08-d810-54b8-b391-27bcd47e0847" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164006 :answer-field/correct "answer-49552c77-e3ef-5aa7-b162-5a1dfbe9d248" :answer-field/choices ["answer-49552c77-e3ef-5aa7-b162-5a1dfbe9d248"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49552c77-e3ef-5aa7-b162-5a1dfbe9d248" :answer/id #uuid "49552c77-e3ef-5aa7-b162-5a1dfbe9d248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164009 :answer-field/correct "answer-e43db76a-b7d9-5afc-a08b-240a4e11be94" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e43db76a-b7d9-5afc-a08b-240a4e11be94"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e43db76a-b7d9-5afc-a08b-240a4e11be94" :answer/id #uuid "e43db76a-b7d9-5afc-a08b-240a4e11be94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164007 :answer-field/correct "answer-ab1c8b15-fac4-5ad5-9509-21b7d131f657" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ab1c8b15-fac4-5ad5-9509-21b7d131f657"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab1c8b15-fac4-5ad5-9509-21b7d131f657" :answer/id #uuid "ab1c8b15-fac4-5ad5-9509-21b7d131f657" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168031 :tutorial/content "In this topic, we'll learn how to use Laplace transforms to solve homogeneous systems like the one below.\n![](images/66/66eb9ce1b87b67ba550fc0b76493b775bf2b2e67be257b9fe9974db9d53cdffa.svg)\n\nThe process can be split into three steps.\n\n- **Step 1.** Apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation, to get a system with variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Solve the obtained system for variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** To find the initial variables\n\n$$\nx_1(t) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad x_2(t)\n$$\n\nsatisfying the original initial value problem, apply the inverse Laplace transform to \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\nLet's see how this works in practice." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167982 :tutorial/content "![](images/44/44a90d0fa61d3643848f01479706cca752a00914b99185da5b8739c5e1cab182.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. In the initial value problem above, we apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation.\n\nFirst, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{5{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=5L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+6L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3=5{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+6{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$\n\n**Step 2**. Now, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns X_1(s) +  3 = 5 X_1(s)\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_1(s) = -\\dfrac{3}{s-5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns X_2(s) -  2 = -2\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{s-5}\\right) + 6 X_2(s) \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**. To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{3}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{8}{s-6}-\\frac{6}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\}-6{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ 8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167006 :activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
